A||||2||kevin||Speedometer not working||||1||
Z||000000||kevin||11-26-2001||03:36 PM||||I started my 1985 4-cyl,5-sp. this morning and glanced at my speedometer. I saw that it was not working(?)!. As a result, my odometer is not registering either.This never happened before.Is there an easy explaination and fix? THanks for your help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||WhiteFieroBlur||11-26-2001||05:23 PM||||well I am far from knowing what wrong but an easy check is the wire in the back near the front bottom of the engine where the transaxle fluid might be unplugged. I took it out one day and forgot to put it back and i was like what?? but plugged it in and I can tell how fast I was going  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eriamjh||11-26-2001||08:23 PM||||Don't know about the automatics, but the manuals have a speed sensor attached (which has the wiring that WhiteFieroBlur described.  If the wiring is hooked up, pull the speed sensor and give it a spin by hand.  It is a nylon gear and could have shattered or cracked.<P>Since the speedo itself is electronic, getting an AC signal fromt the speed sensor, it's not likely to be bad.<P>Probably bad wiring or corrosion.||||reg||1
